# A Term type as the generator derives it: a whole number, an integer, a flag (`wave`), a text, a list, a record of
# named fields, or a choice between types (`pick`). Any value such a type describes is testable with no generator
# written by hand, because the generator is folded from the type.
#
# Ported from deck/test/code/type.ts (cli-in-term-0105). There `genForType` folded a type into a pair of closures,
# `sample` and `shrink`. property-check.tree's `shape` IS that generator, data that `sample-of` and `shrink-of` fold,
# so a type here is built as a shape and `gen-for-type` hands it back as it is. type.ts's convenience constants are
# tasks (traps.md T022, a top-level `host` is private to its module), with the original's names.

load @term/base/list
  find list

load ./property-check
  find shape

# a record's field, as type.ts's `{ name, type }`
form type-field
  link name, like text
  link type, like shape

task t-whole
  like shape

  back make shape/whole

task t-int
  like shape

  back make shape/int

task t-wave
  like shape

  back make shape/wave

task t-text
  like shape

  back make shape/text

task t-list
  take item, like shape
  like shape

  back
    make shape/list
      bind item, item

# a record: one value per field, in the fields' order
task t-record
  take fields, like list, like type-field
  like shape

  host names, make list
  host types, make list
  walk fields
    take each
    names/push(each/name)
    types/push(each/type)

  back
    make shape/record
      bind names, names
      bind types, types

# a union: one of the options, the arm by one draw
task t-pick
  take options, like list, like shape
  like shape

  back
    make shape/pick
      bind options, options

# the generator of a type: the shape itself, which sample-of and shrink-of read
task gen-for-type
  take type, like shape
  like shape

  back type
